Subject: [PATCH 1/2] chore: remove orphan module, extract tool-catalog
 assembly (0.10.338)

Two independent cleanups:

1. Deletes request_lifecycle_context.py. It was added in isolation
   (commit 29050af) and never imported by anything -- confirmed via
   scripts/analyze_imports.py orphan detection. DirectOutcomeContext
   already covers the multi-ContextVar request-scoping case it was
   apparently meant to generalize.

2. Extracts the local-tool catalog assembly out of
   UnifiedMCPAgent._process_user_request into tool_catalog_assembly.py
   (build_request_tool_catalog). This was a straight-line,
   side-effect-free block -- eleven local tool-factory calls plus
   catalog construction -- with no behavior change: same tools, same
   order. mcp_agent_orchestrator.py drops from 1,026 to 999 lines.

Rebased onto origin/main (0.10.337) after upstream independently used
0.10.334/0.10.335 for unrelated fixes (deterministic clarification
choices, deterministic model metadata, live device snapshot caching);
renumbered this change to 0.10.338 to avoid the collision.

This is a first, low-risk step toward splitting the orchestrator, not
the full decomposition -- _process_user_request's confirmation flow,
rule-authoring proposal handling, and the provider tool-calling loop
are still one method and are more deeply coupled to self state.
